--- tick 121 (track D, fifth experiment: Mertens record at N = 10^10) ---
One-liner: raise N in the exact-integer Mertens pipeline (claim #20/#22) from 1e9 to
1e10 to extend the extremal-Mertens record. Why not in DEAD_ENDS: first run of this
pipeline at 1e10; #20 (1e8) and #22 (1e9) are different N. The 1e10 run is the
"extremal Mertens" Track D item; a new record is a NUMERIC record, not an RH witness.
Script changes (git-tracked, output format unchanged so the 1e9 check.sh still passes):
  (1) mu_sieve batches the sign-flip for primes p > N/2 (whose only multiple <= N is
      p itself) into one vectorized op -> cuts the Python loop ~2x; C5 sanity check
      verifies mu[p] goes 1 -> -1 for those primes (direct check of the speed-up).
  (2) del mu after the prefix sum (peak 90GB -> 80GB at N=1e10).
  (3) first_attainment via np.bincount (values bounded by maxabs) -> faster.
  (4) top-10 via a chunked heap -> avoids the ~120GB np.argpartition(-absM) temporary
      that would OOM at N=1e10.
PRIOR-ART PRE-FLIGHT (queries logged):
  Q1: OEIS A084237 (fetched tick 118, saved evidence/2026-08-23-mertens-1e9/
      oeis-a084237-m10n.txt): "a(n) = M(10^n)". a(9) = -222 (matches our 1e9 run),
      a(10) = -33722 => M(10^10) must equal -33722 (F2).
  Q2: OEIS A051402 (fetched tick 118, saved oeis-a051402-def.txt): "smallest k such
      that |M(k)| = n", b-file k=1..10000, a(10000) = 902718903 < 1e10 => firstk[10000]
      must be 902718903 (F3).
  Q3: known Mertens-conjecture counterexample ~1.05e11 (Odlyzko-te Riele 1985, carded)
      => |M(x)| < sqrt(x) still expected to hold at 1e10 (no witness framing needed).
  Conclusion: no published max_{x<=1e10} |M(x)| found; A084237 a(10) + A051402 envelope
  are the cross-checks.
