--- tick 131 (2026-08-23 ~07:00 UTC, frontier) ---
Track D experiment 7: Mertens M(x) scan to 1e11 via SEGMENTED mu sieve
(mertens_segmental.py). Why segmented: full-array mertens_extremal.py needs
~800 GB at N=1e11 (M int32 + absM int32 + mu int8); machine has 125 GB.
Segmented mu: per segment [a,b), mu starts at 1; for each prime p <= sqrt(N):
flip sign at multiples of p, multiply small-radical s(n) by p at multiples of
p, zero mu at multiples of p^2; then n/s(n) > 1 iff n has its one possible
prime factor > sqrt(N) (n <= N => at most one) => flip sign once. Exact ints.

